e control* at `SR_BIG_MB=8` proving the site is really reached), NULL args are compared by **signal number** (SIGSEGV=11), and the two non-termination rows assert both libraries are *still running* after 3 s and then kill them.\n\n## Phase D — parity, configs, anti-vacuity\n\n- `nm -D` diff is **empty** for release *and* debug Rust `.so`; undefined symbols are libc/libgcc only.\n- `scripts/verify_all.sh`: 6 symbol-parity checks + 9 suite runs = {default, `--no-default-features`, `--all-features`} × {release `.so`, debug `.so`, debug harness} → **ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASS** (the crate has no `[features]`, so the combos are enumerated and run explicitly).\n- `scripts/mutation_check.sh`: 9 injected bugs (overlapping restart, empty-needle handling, wrong `strdup` arg, removed OOM check, off-by-one gap/tail copies, truncating `strncpy`, last-match `strstr`, skipped prefix copy) — **9/9 detected**, `src/lib.rs` restored bit-identically (md5-verified).\n\n**No divergence was found**: the existing Rust translation is byte-identical to the C across every row, including the C's quirks (it hangs on an empty needle exactly like the C, leaks-and-returns-`NULL` on allocation failure, and never re-scans replacement text). Only `Cargo.toml` gained `libloading` as a dev-dependency; `c_src/` sources are untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":692,"cache_read_input_tokens":143520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":692,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f66ff6-65d9-4ed7-bcee-7095c304cf98","uuid":"bfefdb00-d186-4f4b-8674-fa867ac9b76c","timestamp":"2026-08-27T16:30:28.081Z"}
